cdcacm: no class-specific protocol on the communication interface

Purpose: the CDC ACM communication interface reported bInterfaceProtocol 1
(AT commands, V.250), which makes ModemManager treat the console as a modem
candidate.  Report 0 (no class-specific protocol).
Zephyr: the Zephyr build's CDC ACM communication interface uses protocol 0
(subsys/usb/device_next/class/usbd_cdc_acm.c, bInterfaceProtocol = 0).

diff --git a/drivers/usbdev/cdcacm_desc.c b/drivers/usbdev/cdcacm_desc.c
index 40f3d785..d34bee87 100644
--- a/drivers/usbdev/cdcacm_desc.c
+++ b/drivers/usbdev/cdcacm_desc.c
@@ -600,7 +600,7 @@ int16_t cdcacm_mkcfgdesc(FAR uint8_t *buf,
 #endif
       dest->classid  = USB_CLASS_CDC;                        /* Interface class */
       dest->subclass = CDC_SUBCLASS_ACM;                     /* Interface sub-class */
-      dest->protocol = CDC_PROTO_ATM;                        /* Interface protocol */
+      dest->protocol = CDC_PROTO_NONE;                       /* Interface protocol */
 #ifdef CONFIG_CDCACM_NOTIFSTR
       dest->iif      = devinfo->strbase + CDCACM_NOTIFSTRID; /* iInterface */
 #else
